<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Madanda</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1890 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Shona kingdom in central Mozambique between the Buzi and Save rivers, on the edge of the Mutapa and Uteve world.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Madanda emerged around 1500 as one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shona">Shona</a>-speaking states between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a> and the coast, south of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-uteve">Kingdom of Uteve</a>. Its rulers were probably linked by origin to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> dynasty, but the kingdom appears only occasionally in Portuguese records.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its government. Like its neighbours, it was probably ruled by a sacred king advised by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spirit-medium">spirit mediums</a>, and its people farmed, herded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> and traded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> and gold with Portuguese posts at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofala">Sofala</a> and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 19th century Madanda came under the domination of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaza-empire">Gaza Nguni</a> state. In the 1890s its territory passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mozambique-company">Mozambique Company</a> and was absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/portuguese-mozambique">Portuguese Mozambique</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1890 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central and Southern Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.55%;width:7.76%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1890 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional Shona religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Shona (Ndau)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mozambique">Mozambique</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Danda, Madanda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1695&amp;focus=kingdom-of-madanda" aria-label="Kingdom of Madanda on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5717 2689 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Madanda lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5833 3185h0M5880 3217h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6037 2945h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6037 2945h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Mozambique. <a href="/atlas?year=1695&amp;focus=kingdom-of-madanda">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
